page('05 / Architecture and retrieval design')
table([['Stage','Design'],['1. Ingest','CSV facts remain structured; Markdown headers supply metadata'],['2. Chunk','One section per bracketed ID; retain source file and dates'],['3. Filter','Only status=current and effective_from on/before dataset date'],['4. Retrieve','70% word TF-IDF similarity + 30% character TF-IDF similarity'],['5. Re-rank','Authority multipliers; concept-based policy priors of +0.18'],['6. Control','Session controller decides verification, facts or escalation'],['7. Respond','Extractive policy excerpts or deterministic factual response'],['8. Audit','Evidence IDs, evaluation CSV and real mock-tool result']],[100,400])
h('Why an extractive baseline?')
p('The system runs without external inference APIs, paid tokens or an embedding service. Character n-grams help with noisy spellings; word bigrams capture short phrases. A small synonym map links customer expressions such as send it back, collect and torn to return, reverse pickup and damage. Limited Hindi/Hinglish terms are expanded into English retrieval concepts.')
h('Policy authority and versioning')
p('Policy similarity scores are multiplied by 1.3, agent guides by 1.1, help by 1.0, FAQs by 0.65 and marketing by 0.4. These are transparent engineering heuristics, not learned probabilities. Superseded returns v3 is excluded from retrieval; current RET-3 explicitly states the pre-August electronics exception. Scoring alone cannot guarantee that lower-authority content will never conflict with policy.')
h('Abstention and citations')
p('A maximum score below 0.12 produces a lack-of-information response with an offer of human help. Otherwise the system returns up to three labeled source excerpts. Because business-concept priors can raise irrelevant matches above threshold, unsupported-question detection requires stronger future calibration.')
page('06 / Private workflows and business rules')
h('Identity-gated state machine')
p('Order ID received &rarr; unverified lookup &rarr; request one proof &rarr; verify phone suffix or delivery pincode &rarr; disclose only on success. Two failed attempts lock the active order in that session. Switching to a different order clears authorization. Browser sessions use opaque cookie tokens; a reset clears conversation state.')
p('This is educational identity checking only. Pincodes and phone suffixes are weak secrets, and resetting or switching orders bypasses the local retry counter. Real deployments need stronger authentication, persistent rate limits and formal session expiry.')
h('Date conventions')
p('All business calculations use 20 October 2026, not the report date. Business days are Monday through Saturday excluding the four listed holidays. business_add excludes the start date. A card refund initiated 17 October reaches its 5th business day on 24 October and 7th on 27 October: 18 October is Sunday and 19 October is a warehouse closure.')
p('Return deadlines use delivery date plus the policy window in calendar days, with the boundary treated as inclusive. Electronics delivered before 1 August retain 10 days; later deliveries use 7. Eligible fashion orders placed 1-15 October receive 30 days. An ambiguous multi-item request asks for the SKU. Condition requirements still apply; a calculated date is not an approved return.')
h('Escalation and action honesty')
p('Selected explicit triggers include safety risks, legal complaints, unauthorized activity, human-agent requests, repeat contacts, high-value damage and overdue refunds. A ticket is announced only if create_ticket returns created=True. The tool writes a local synthetic ticket, not a real CRM entry. Cancellation responses guide the customer to My Orders; the assistant never performs a cancellation.')
p('Free-form customer text is not placed in handover summaries to avoid echoing secrets. This safety choice sacrifices some contextual detail required by ESC-3 and must be improved with tested redaction before production.')
page('07 / Evaluation method and results')
img('retrieval_performance.png',495,205)
p('For each question with policy evidence, Recall@k is the fraction of required KB section IDs present in the first k results. The report macro-averages across 47 evidence-bearing questions. Structured CSV evidence is excluded, so these scores do not evaluate catalog joins. Five unanswerable questions remain in the exported row-level file but are excluded from policy-evidence recall.')
p('MRR@5 uses the reciprocal rank of the first relevant policy section within five results, or zero when absent. The original text and supplied ASR-like text are evaluated separately against the same labels. ASR-like strings are not audio recordings and do not measure speech recognition quality.')
