p('Small slice sizes make these percentages unstable. The hi-en slice does not demonstrate fluent Hinglish output: it measures required policy IDs appearing in retrieval, not linguistic quality. English-first excerpts remain a known usability limitation.')
h('Failure modes')
p('Macro Recall@5 of 70.21% leaves substantial evidence uncovered. Lexical mismatch, multi-source questions and translated queries remain difficult. Authority multipliers do not prove contradiction-free answers; top-five evaluation also differs from the three excerpts shown in general responses. High-value matching uses catalog price, not an adjudicated paid-item value. Unstructured date and safety wording outside the rule vocabulary may be missed.')
